      "text": "Under the Labor Code, any shortfall in hours worked on a given day (undertime) cannot be cancelled out by overtime worked on another day; the employer must still pay the overtime premium separately. Overtime is only payable for work beyond eight hours in a day and must include at least a 25% premium over the regular wage.",
