      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Overtime work is allowed only after the regular eight‑hour day, and the employee must receive extra pay equal to the regular wage plus at least 25 % of that wage; on holidays or rest days the premium rises to at least 30 % of the regular wage. These rates apply to all private‑sector workers unless they fall under the specific exemptions listed in the rules.",
