      "text": "If you work beyond eight hours on a regular workday, you are entitled to your regular wage plus at least 25% extra, unless the overtime is one of the specific situations listed in the compulsory overtime provision; in those cases the employer may require the extra hours but must still pay the 25% premium. The key fact to determine is whether the rush‑order work fits any of the enumerated cases such as urgent work to avoid loss or damage to the employer’s property or to finish work started before the eighth hour.",
