    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "The general overtime framework says that any employee who works beyond eight hours on an ordinary day must be paid his regular wage plus at least 25% extra, and the same 25% rate applies under the Labor Code as well; higher rates apply only for work on holidays or rest days. To apply the rule you need to confirm that the extra hours were worked on a regular workday and not on a holiday or rest day.",
      "evidence": [
