      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Overtime work is paid at the regular wage plus at least 25 % for any employee who works beyond eight hours in a day, but an employer may only require overtime if the situation falls under one of the specific cases listed (such as war, emergency, urgent work to avoid loss, etc.); if none of those apply, the employee cannot be forced to work past eight hours.",
