      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Labor Code, an employment is treated as regular only when the work is part of the employer’s usual business, but it is considered casual if it is fixed for a specific project whose completion or termination was determined at the time of hiring; if the contract does not state when the project will end, the default classification is casual. To verify the status, you should check whether the contract includes a definite project‑completion date or term, because without that detail the employment remains casual and the employee does not automatically acquire regular‑employee security of tenure.",
