      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "In a SEnA conciliation meeting, the dispute must be filed where the party first sought help—either the DOLE, NCMB, or NLRC—and the conciliator will run through a step‑by‑step process: first clarifying the issues and positions, then narrowing the points of disagreement, encouraging the parties to propose settlement options, offering mutually acceptable proposals, and finally facilitating a settlement agreement while monitoring compliance. All labor‑related cases are subject to this mandatory conciliation‑mediation, and the labor arbiter or the appropriate DOLE office will only handle cases that have been properly endorsed, though either side may end the conciliation early and ask for referral or arbitration. Participants must attend the meetings, avoid any act that disrupts settlement, and the proceedings are privileged, meaning the conciliator cannot be called to testify about what was discussed.",      
