      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Consumer Act, the maker or importer of a rice cooker is liable for any defect in the product and must provide sufficient information on how to use it safely and what hazards may be involved; if the switch is faulty, the defect‑related liability applies regardless of fault, unless the seller can prove the product was not placed on the market, had no defect, or the consumer caused the problem.",
