      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "An employer who wants to dismiss a worker must give the worker a written notice that spells out the specific acts or omissions that justify the dismissal; without that written notice, the dismissal does not meet the procedural requirement under the labor rules. The grounds for dismissal must also be among the just causes listed in Article 283 of the Labor Code.",
