    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Selling a refurbished tablet while representing it as new is a deceptive sales practice prohibited by law, because a seller may not claim a consumer product is new, original, or unused when it is actually reconditioned or second‑hand. Such false representation falls within the list of deceptive acts defined in the Consumer Act.",
