      "text": "An employer may only deduct from your wages if you are clearly shown to be responsible for the loss or damage, you are given a reasonable chance to contest it, the deduction is fair and does not exceed the actual loss, and the total deduction stays within 20 % of your weekly wages; otherwise, any withholding of wages without your consent is unlawful.",
