      "text": "Under the Consumer Act, any manufacturer, producer or importer is liable for damages caused by a defective product regardless of fault; a product is defective when it fails to provide the safety that a consumer rightfully expects, considering its presentation, the reasonably expected use and hazards, and the time it was placed on the market. To determine liability, you must establish whether the extension cord’s exposed live wiring makes it unsafe under those criteria and whether the seller can prove that it did not place the product on the market, that the product had no defect, or that the consumer was solely at fault.",
